                    <msContents>
                        <summary>A copy of the story entitled The Romance of Saif Dhu
                            l-Yazan.</summary>
                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14380_item_1">
                            <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="">Ḥikāyat Sayf dhī al-Yazan
                                al-Ḥaḍramī</title>
                            <title xml:lang="ar" type="alt">حكاية سيف ذي اليزن الحضرمي</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en">The Romance of Sayif dhi Yazan</title>

                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                            <note>
                                <p>The text of the story differs from that of Bulāq and Cairo
                                    editions, and also from the manuscripts British Library ii, 1172
                                    and Berlin 9119, to judge from the qutations given therein. The
                                    tale is complete in the manuscripts, and includes the full plot.
                                    It ends with the death of Miṣr from grief at the loss of the
                                    magical bead that Farḥān, his servant, had swallowed.</p>
                                <p>Colophon on <locus from="243b">folio 243b</locus> gives the date
                                    and place of production.</p>
                                <p>For another copy, see <ref
                                        target="https://searcharchives.bl.uk/catalog/032-003945799"
                                        >British Library Or 4643</ref>, <ref
                                        target="https://archive.org/details/supplementtocata00brituoft/page/740/mode/2up"
                                        >Rieu, C. <title>Supplement to the catalogue of the Arabic
                                            manuscripts in the British Museum</title> (London,
                                        1894)</ref>, p. 740, no. 1172. </p>
                            </note>
                            <colophon>قد كتبه محليه بغيه وقلمه الفقير ... الحاج احمد نظيف ابن
                                المرحوم ... حثمان خوجه الجزاثرى المقيم بالقسطنطينية ... وذلك فى محرح
                                الحرام سنة سبع وخمسين ومائتان والف.</colophon>
                            <incipit>الحمد لله رب العالمين ... اما بعد فان محا يرغب فيه ذوو الالباب </incipit>
                            <explicit>محا يوجب الاستغراب وقد استوفينا على ايامه الكلام فليكن هذا
                                منتهى المرام</explicit>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
